  "saferAlternatives": [
    "Names, comments and types live in borer's session and never touch the binary; the naming and typing tools preview until called with dry_run=false.",
    "fetch_pdb downloads from Microsoft's symbol server, or from BORER_SYMBOL_SERVER when set; set it only to a server you trust, and keep the PDB cache local.",
    "Live tools read memory of a running process of the loaded binary (Windows), never writing it; leave BORER_LIVE_ANY unset so no other process can be read.",
    "Point BORER_OUTPUT_DIR at a scratch folder: every project or C file a tool writes lands under it, and an existing one is replaced only when the call says overwrite."
  ]
